# Creativity is Engineering

You are working in a methodology repo. Prefer writing invariants, case studies, and probes over generating more code.

- No timing data → do not optimize "slow".
- One failure kind → exactly one action. Never treat all errors as retry.
- Stop signals are explicit (STOP). "Recent failures" is not a stop signal.
- Secrets never go in installers. Config is URL + paste + IP.
- If the operator says a behavior is an advantage, record it as an invariant. Do not "fix" it.
- Insights from a chat must land in `patterns/` or `case-studies/` in the same change.
- First commit on a behavior change is a failing test that uses real failure text.

Read `prompts/diagnose-first.md` before implementing.
